2. Abstract

The Bio‑Integrity Simulation System (BISS‑v1.0) is a sovereign‑grade biomedical computation engine designed to model human physiology under full encryption while autonomously validating the integrity of every computational transition. The system integrates encrypted telemetry, anonymized clinical datasets, multi‑compartment metabolic modeling, pharmacokinetic‑pharmacodynamic (PK/PD) simulation, and a sovereign suprakernel that enforces correctness, detects tampering, and validates physiological transitions. BISS‑v1.0 enables tamper‑proof, privacy‑preserving medical computation suitable for clinical trials, precision medicine, critical care, and global epidemiology.

3. Introduction

Biomedical computation today is fragmented across telemetry systems, PK/PD solvers, EHR infrastructures, and AI diagnostic tools. These systems expose raw patient data, lack autonomous integrity validation, and are vulnerable to drift, corruption, and unauthorized modification.

BISS‑v1.0 introduces a unified architecture where physiology, encryption, and integrity coexist as a single computational organism. By embedding endogenous encryption and suprakernel‑validated transitions into the modeling pipeline, BISS‑v1.0 establishes a new category: sovereign encrypted biomedical simulation.

